---
/**
 * Eine Wertung aus Teamkollegen-Duellen.
 *
 * Die einzige Seite dieses Projekts, die ein Modell zeigt statt einer
 * Zählung. Deshalb steht hier mehr Text als sonst: Was eine Zahl bedeutet und
 * was sie nicht bedeutet, muss neben ihr stehen, sonst wird aus einer Rechnung
 * eine Behauptung.
 */
import Seite from '../../layouts/Seite.astro'
import { zahl } from '../../lib/format.js'
import { db, pfad } from '../../lib/db.js'
import { rangliste, zusammenhang } from '../../engine/duell.js'

const MIN = 30
const rennen = rangliste(db(), { art: 'rennen', minDuelle: MIN, anzahl: 30 })
const quali = rangliste(db(), { art: 'qualifying', minDuelle: MIN, anzahl: 30 })
const netz = zusammenhang(db(), 'rennen')

const quote = (v) => `${Math.round(v * 100)}%`
---

<Seite
  titel="Team-mate ratings – drivers measured against the same car"
  beschreibung="A rating built only from duels between team-mates, who shared the same car. A model, not a measurement – with its assumptions stated."
>
  <h1>Team-mates</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    The hardest question in this sport is how good a driver was, independent of the car. It
    cannot be measured. But there is one comparison that needs no assumption about machinery:
    two team-mates drove the same car, so whoever finished ahead says something about the
    drivers.
  </p>

  <div class="warnung">
    <b>This is a model, not a count.</b>
    <p>
      Everything else on this site is counted from the results. This page is not: it runs a
      chess-style rating over {zahl(netz.fahrer)} drivers and their team-mate duels. The
      ranking depends on three assumptions, and all three are only roughly true.
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <b>Team-mates get equal machinery.</b> Often, but not always – there were first and
        second drivers, and teams that favoured a title contender.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Strength carries over.</b> If A beat B and B beat C, the rating treats A as stronger
        than C. Hamilton raced Alonso, Alonso raced Fisichella, Fisichella raced Button – that
        is how eras connect here. Over long chains the error accumulates.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>A duel is a fair test.</b> A retirement is not, so only races where both finished
        count. A pit-stop error or a first-lap collision still distorts one.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="schluss">
      {zahl(netz.groessteGruppe)} of the {zahl(netz.fahrer)} drivers are connected into a single
      chain, so most of these numbers are comparable with each other. Drivers with fewer than
      {' '}{MIN} duels are left out: after three duels a rating still sits close to where it
      started, and listing such a driver next to Hamilton would mislead.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="raster">
    <section>
      <h2>Race duels</h2>
      <p class="hinweis">Who finished ahead, in races where both team-mates were classified.</p>
      <div class="tabelle">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th class="num">#</th><th>Driver</th><th class="num">Rating</th>
              <th class="num">Duels</th><th class="num">Won</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {rennen.map((r, i) => (
              <tr>
                <td class="num rang">{i + 1}</td>
                <td>
                  <a class="zeile" href={pfad.fahrer(r.id)}>{r.name}</a>
                  <span class="neben">{r.von}–{r.bis} · {r.gegner} team-mates</span>
                </td>
                <td class="num stark">{r.wertung}</td>
                <td class="num">{r.duelle}</td>
                <td class="num">{quote(r.quote)}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Qualifying duels</h2>
      <p class="hinweis">
        Who was quicker over one lap. Strategy and traffic play no part, which makes this the
        cleaner comparison of the two – and it is not the same ranking.
      </p>
      <div class="tabelle">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th class="num">#</th><th>Driver</th><th class="num">Rating</th>
              <th class="num">Duels</th><th class="num">Won</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {quali.map((r, i) => (
              <tr>
                <td class="num rang">{i + 1}</td>
                <td>
                  <a class="zeile" href={pfad.fahrer(r.id)}>{r.name}</a>
                  <span class="neben">{r.von}–{r.bis} · {r.gegner} team-mates</span>
                </td>
                <td class="num stark">{r.wertung}</td>
                <td class="num">{r.duelle}</td>
                <td class="num">{quote(r.quote)}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section>
    <h2>How it is worked out</h2>
    <div class="methode">
      <p>
        Every driver starts at 1500. After each duel the winner takes points from the loser, and
        how many depends on what was expected: beating a much stronger team-mate moves the
        rating far, beating a much weaker one barely at all. It is the chess rating, unchanged –
        nothing about it is specific to motor racing.
      </p>
      <p>
        <b>Indianapolis is left out.</b> The Indy 500 counted towards the World Championship from
        1950 to 1960, but it was a separate race with its own regulations and its own entry – and,
        decisively here, the constructor there is the chassis builder, not the team. In 1955
        Kurtis Kraft supplied 23 of the 35 cars. Those 23 drivers were not team-mates but
        independent entrants who had bought the same chassis; counted as duels, that one race
        alone would produce 253 false comparisons. Leaving it out costs 1,867 of 8,854 duels.
      </p>
      <p>
        <b>Read the number of duels beside the rating.</b> It is the honest measure of how much
        the rating is worth. A driver with 30 duels against two team-mates is placed on thinner
        evidence than one with 300 against fourteen.
      </p>
      <p class="weiter">
        Every driver's own team-mate record, race by race, is on their page under
        {' '}<a href={pfad.seite('/drivers/')}>Drivers</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Seite>

<style>
  .warnung {
    max-width: 52rem;
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0;
    padding: 1rem 1.15rem;
    background: var(--surface-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--warn);
    border-radius: 0.6rem;
  }

  .warnung > b { color: var(--ink); font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .warnung p { margin: 0.5rem 0 0; font-size: 0.87rem; color: var(--ink-2); text-wrap: pretty; }
  .warnung ol { margin: 0.75rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; display: grid; gap: 0.4rem; }
  .warnung li { font-size: 0.87rem; color: var(--ink-2); text-wrap: pretty; }
  .warnung li b { color: var(--ink); }
  .warnung .schluss { padding-top: 0.75rem; margin-top: 0.75rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--muted); }

  .raster {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(24rem, 100%), 1fr));
    gap: 2rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }

  h2 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 0 0 0.4rem; }

  .hinweis {
    max-width: 30rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.83rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  td.rang { color: var(--muted); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; width: 2rem; }
  td.stark { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 650; }
  td .neben { display: block; font-size: 0.74rem; color: var(--muted); }

  section { margin-top: 2.5rem; }

  .methode {
    max-width: 52rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.15rem;
    background: var(--surface-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0.6rem;
  }

  .methode p { margin: 0 0 0.75rem; font-size: 0.86rem; color: var(--ink-2); text-wrap: pretty; }
  .methode p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .methode b { color: var(--ink); }
  .weiter { padding-top: 0.75rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--muted) !important; }
</style>
